  "id": "sequential-effect",
  "term": "sequential effect",
  "definition": "A sequential effect is the influence of an earlier judgment or preference on the one that comes next. In this context, a person’s preference for a previous stimulus can shift preference for a later stimulus, often in the same direction.",
